  "report_text": "The monthly number of solar flares increased steadily from February 2021 to February 2026.\nThe busiest month was February 2022, with 1,234 flares.\nThe share of strong flares (M/X class) rose from 12% in 2021 to 24% in 2025, indicating a growing trend.\nThis increase suggests that the intensity of solar activity is rising over time.\nStrong flares were more frequent in later years, particularly in 2024 and 2025.\nThe data shows a consistent upward trend in both total flares and strong flares.\nThe highest monthly count was observed in February 2022."
